    correctAnswers: ["C"],
    rationale: "Retry-with-error-feedback works because the model sees what it produced, what was wrong, and the source to correct against. And the boundary matters: format and structural errors are retryable; information absent from the document is not. Why not the others: A retries blind — the model can't fix errors it isn't shown; B removes the document and extraction the correction must reference; D abandons the failed extraction rather than repairing it.",
