    rationale: "custom_id exists for exactly this: correlate failures to their source documents, fix what caused each failure (chunk the oversized ones), and resubmit only the fixed subset — paying again for 200 documents, not 10,000. Why not the others: B reprocesses 9,800 successes to retry 200 failures; C silently drops 2% of the corpus; D misunderstands context limits, which belong to the model, not the API path — unchunked oversized documents fail synchronously too.",
