    correctAnswers: ["A"],
    rationale: "Compiling a structured handoff with what's already been found — customer, order, and the identified issue — before escalating preserves the investigation and hands the human a ready-to-act case. Why not the others: B defers the work of surfacing the relevant details to whoever follows the reference ID, adding friction; C discards everything the agent already discovered; D attempts an action known to be out of scope, risking a policy violation instead of deterministically escalating it.",
