    correctAnswers: ["B"],
    rationale: "A timeout genuinely leaves delivery status unknown — it may have succeeded. Saying so explicitly, and advising against retry, is the only response that matches reality and prevents duplicate sends. Why not the others: A mislabels an unknown outcome as safely retryable, when retrying an already-possibly-sent message is precisely the problem; C actively encourages the behavior causing duplicates; D re-echoes the message without addressing the retry-safety question at all.",
