    rationale: "Putting the likely cause and concrete troubleshooting steps directly in the error response gives the agent everything it needs to help the user in a single turn, with no extra round trip. Why not the others: A hands the agent raw technical fields it has no way to translate into user-facing guidance; B works but adds an unnecessary extra tool call for information that could simply ride along in the original error; C misrepresents a failure as a success, which will mislead the user about the device's actual state.",
