    rationale: "Exposing 50+ tools simultaneously degrades selection accuracy regardless of how well each is described; dynamically scoping down to only the 2-3 connectors that actually match the current need turns an overloaded decision into an easy one. Why not the others: A is a reactive band-aid that lets the wrong-tool error happen and then recovers, rather than preventing it; B helps marginally but 50+ simultaneously active tools still cause systemic overload; D removes the agent's ability to inspect and choose correctly among subtly different connector variants.",
    topicTag: "Dynamic Tool Scoping at Scale",
